Preserve the exact writable environment across loader handoff. Restoring an
absent LD_LIBRARY_PATH as an empty string both adds an undeclared variable and,
with upstream's read-only literal, causes environment-writing programs to fault.

The temporary entry is appended: restore its null terminator instead. Existing
entries retain their original writable strings. No allocation or stack copying
is added, and loader-time library-profile lookup is unchanged.

Upstream issue/PR draft (not filed): Preserve the exact writable environment
across loader handoff. Remove when pinned upstream includes both fixes.

diff --git a/src/main.rs b/src/main.rs
--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -42,3 +42,2 @@
 const DEFAULT_NIX_LD_LIBRARY_PATH: &[u8] = b"/run/current-system/sw/share/nix-ld/lib";
-const EMPTY_LD_LIBRARY_PATH_ENV: &CStr = c"LD_LIBRARY_PATH=";
 
@@ -167,13 +166,9 @@
-        // If the entry trampoline is available on the platform, LD_LIBRARY_PATH
-        // will be replaced with an empty LD_LIBRARY_PATH when ld.so launches
-        // the actual program.
-        //
-        // We cannot replace it with NIX_LD_LIBRARY_PATH as it would take
-        // precedence over config files.
+        // The temporary variable was appended to the environment vector.
+        // Restore its terminating null instead of exposing a new variable.
         EnvEdit {
             entry: ptr::null(),
-            old_string: EMPTY_LD_LIBRARY_PATH_ENV.as_ptr().cast(),
+            old_string: ptr::null(),
         }
     };
 
